+## Extension-specific chord component labels and layout
+
+This section describes the independently maintained Fumen Language Support patch, not the published Fumen 1.3.3 API.
+
+The renderer can change chord-symbol labels without changing chord notation, parsing, or transposition. The default settings below reproduce the original compact rendering. The minor default is an en dash (`–`, U+2013); the major default is a Greek capital delta (`Δ`, U+0394), not the white triangle character (`△`).
+
+| Parameter | Default | Description |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `minor_label` | `"–"` | Text used for a minor triad. |
+| `major_label` | `"Δ"` | Text used for an explicit major mark. |
+| `diminished_label` | `"O"` | Text used for a diminished triad. The default is capital O; choose `"dim"` for letters. |
+| `half_diminished_label` | `"Ø"` | Text replacing the whole minor-seventh-flat-fifth combination. Choose `"m7-5"` for both `Cm7-5` and `Cm7b5`. Independent of `minor_label`. |
+| `augmented_label` | `"+"` | Text used for an augmented triad. Choose `"aug"` for both `Caug` and `C+`. |
+| `chord_suffix_style` | `"compact"` | `"compact"` keeps Fumen's small upper/lower components. `"inline"` draws every component after the root at the normal size and baseline. |
+
+```fumen
+%PARAM={"minor_label":"–","major_label":"Δ","diminished_label":"O","half_diminished_label":"Ø","augmented_label":"+","chord_suffix_style":"compact"}
+| Am7(#11)/C | AM7/E | Cdim7 | Cm7-5 | Caug | C+ |
+```
+
+For letter-based inline chord symbols, select the labels and inline style. This applies consistently to chord qualities, extensions, fifths, parenthesized alterations, and a right-positioned slash bass.
+
+```fumen
+%PARAM={"minor_label":"m","major_label":"M","diminished_label":"dim","half_diminished_label":"m7-5","augmented_label":"aug","chord_suffix_style":"inline"}
+| Am7(#11)/C | AM7/E | Cdim7 | Cm7-5 | Caug | C+ |
+```
+
+These labels standardize each chord quality, not the source spelling. They do not add input notation such as `CØ` or `C°`; use `Cm7-5` and `Cdim`. Non-string labels fall back to their defaults. The whole half-diminished label uses one size and baseline, including in compact mode. All multi-character quality labels, including `"min"` and `"maj"`, use their natural width. Inline augmented labels precede extensions (`Caug7` / `C+7`).
+
+When `on_bass_style` is `"below"`, the bass remains below the chord as requested, but uses the inline font size when `chord_suffix_style` is `"inline"`.
+
 
 Also, chord symbols can be specified followed by duration indicator. Please see the section of [duration indicator](duration-indicator.md).
 
