+
+## Extension-specific lyric rules
+
+These rules belong to the independently maintained Fumen Language Support patch, not the published Fumen 1.3.3.
+
+If no chord follows the atmark in the measure, a lyric is attached to the first rhythm slash (`./.`) or rest after it and drawn below it. The published Fumen drops it.
+In a lyric, `\/` is an ordinary slash and `\\` an ordinary backslash; any other backslash is kept, and an unescaped `/` still starts a new row.
+
+| Markdown | Description |
+| -------- | ----------- |
+| \`still here\`@ ./. | A lyric below a rhythm slash. |
+| \`and\\/or\`@ C | One row, "and/or". |
